1 CLEAR

   Clears the machine's memory or the console's string pool.

   Format

     CLEAR keyword

   Breakpoints, interrupts, the translation buffer, and the machine's
   symbol table are the debugger's: see CANCEL in the debugger's help
   (DEBUG, then HELP CANCEL).  A DCL symbol is deleted with
   DELETE/SYMBOL.

2 MEMORY

   Sets all of physical memory to zeros, which clears virtual memory
   too, and turns memory management off, since the page tables are
   gone.  ZERO is the same.  VMINIT lays virtual memory out again.

   Format

     CLEAR MEMORY

2 STRINGS

   Empties the string pool (see SHOW STRING_POOL).  The descriptors
   already made from it are no longer good, so clear it only when the
   programs that use them are gone from memory.

   Format

     CLEAR STRINGS
